---
import SiteLink from '../../components/SiteLink.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/VentureLayout.astro';
import Art from '../../components/Art.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import VentureMap from '../../components/VentureMap.astro';

---
<Layout section="overview" title="Venture Launchpad — turn an idea into evidence" description="Explore a practical venture-building journey: problem discovery, customer validation, business models, MVPs and pilot learning. Share a non-confidential idea brief.">
<section slot="hero" class="container launchpad-hero"><div class="launchpad-intro"><p class="eyebrow">VENTURE LAUNCHPAD · STARTUP ADVISORY</p><h1>From idea to execution.<br/><span>One useful decision<br/>at a time.</span></h1><p class="lede">Find the problem worth solving. Test the opportunity. Shape an MVP and agree the support needed to bring it to life.</p><div class="actions"><SiteLink class="button" href="/venture-studio/submit/">Share your idea <Icon name="lightbulb"/></SiteLink><SiteLink class="text-link" href="/venture-studio/journey/">Explore the advisory journey <Icon name="arrowRight"/></SiteLink></div><p class="caption">For founders and early teams. Start with a non-confidential brief.</p></div><div class="launchpad-workspace"><Art name="venture-studio" alt="AI-generated illustration of an early team discussing a venture; not an actual client engagement" priority/><article class="decision-brief"><p class="eyebrow"><Icon name="file"/> AN EXAMPLE WORKING BRIEF</p><h2>Before we build, what must we learn?</h2><dl><div><dt><Icon name="search"/>The problem</dt><dd>A specific difficulty for a specific user.</dd></div><div><dt><Icon name="flask"/>The experiment</dt><dd>A small test of the riskiest assumption.</dd></div><div><dt><Icon name="compass"/>The next decision</dt><dd>Proceed, revise or pause based on evidence.</dd></div></dl><span class="caption">Illustrative advisory document, not client progress.</span></article></div></section>
<section class="container section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">START WHERE YOU ARE</p><h2>You don’t need a polished pitch.</h2></div><p>A clear problem, a user you want to understand and a willingness to test assumptions are useful starting points. A prototype or early customer feedback can make the conversation more concrete.</p></div><div class="three-grid">{[['search','A problem you keep noticing','Describe what is difficult today, who experiences it and how they currently cope. Specific observations are more useful than a large market claim.'],['layers','A prototype with open questions','Bring an early demo or concept and the question it is meant to answer. We can explore what needs validation before more features are built.'],['users','A team ready to learn','Student groups and early founders can share their strengths, constraints and the support they are looking for. A venture can draw on several engineering disciplines.']].map(([icon,title,copy])=><article class="feature"><span class="feature-icon"><Icon name={icon}/></span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="container section section-tight"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">CHOOSE THE SUPPORT YOU NEED</p><h2>A working relationship,<br/>shaped around your next milestone.</h2></div><p>The starting point depends on your evidence and constraints. Each engagement needs an agreed scope, responsibilities and a useful definition of completion.</p></div><div class="three-grid">{[['message','Advisory sessions','Work through the problem, customer assumptions, business model or delivery options. Leave with decisions, open questions and the next useful task.','A decision note and next-step plan'],['flask','Validation workbench','Plan customer conversations, a prototype experiment or an early pilot. Decide what evidence would change your direction before investing further.','An experiment brief and evidence review'],['code','MVP & execution planning','Translate a validated opportunity into architecture, milestones and ownership. Implementation support is scoped separately around agreed capabilities and availability.','An MVP scope, delivery plan and handover criteria']].map(([icon,title,copy,output])=><article class="feature advisory-option"><span class="feature-icon"><Icon name={icon}/></span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p><div class="advisory-output"><strong>Example working output</strong><p>{output}</p></div></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="container section section-tight"><VentureMap/></section>
<section class="container section two-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">A SIMPLE FIRST CONVERSATION</p><h2>Share the idea.<br />Agree the next step.</h2><p>Start with a short, non-confidential brief. The academy reviews fit and available support; where there is a useful next conversation, the team can follow up by email.</p><p>Advisory sessions, research support, technical architecture, prototype implementation and execution support can be scoped separately. Responsibilities, fees, delivery milestones and any external specialists are agreed before work begins. Submitting an idea does not guarantee selection, funding, investment or an incubation place.</p></div><article class="readiness-card"><h3>What happens after a brief?</h3><ol class="numbered-steps"><li>Understand the problem, intended user and current stage.</li><li>Discuss evidence, constraints and the help you need.</li><li>If mutually suitable, agree an advisory or execution scope, owners and milestones.</li><li>Review progress, decisions and handover through email and shared working documents.</li></ol><p>Working documents and review conversations keep decisions visible. The illustrated journey shows how an engagement could work; it does not show the status of a submitted idea.</p></article></section>
<section class="container section section-tight"><div class="cta-panel"><div><p class="eyebrow light">YOUR NEXT USEFUL EXPERIMENT</p><h2>What are you trying to change?</h2><p>Start with a short idea brief. Share enough to explain the problem; keep confidential implementation details out of the initial submission.</p></div><SiteLink class="button white" href="/venture-studio/submit/">Share your idea <Icon name="arrowUpRight" /></SiteLink></div></section></Layout>
<style>.launchpad-hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:42px;padding-top:35px;padding-bottom:30px;align-items:start}.launchpad-intro{padding-top:24px}.launchpad-intro h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,3.5vw,3.2rem);line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:22px 0}.launchpad-intro h1 span{color:#315e87}.launchpad-intro .lede{font-size:1rem;max-width:550px}.launchpad-intro .caption{margin-top:20px}.launchpad-workspace{position:relative;padding-bottom:30px}.launchpad-workspace :global(.art img){border-radius:28px 28px 9px 28px;width:100%;aspect-ratio:2.35;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 12%;box-shadow:0 16px 40px #18355812}.decision-brief{position:relative;background:#fff;border:1px solid #dce7ef;border-radius:14px;padding:20px;margin:12px 20px 0 45px;box-shadow:0 12px 28px #19395612}.decision-brief .eyebrow{display:flex;gap:9px;align-items:center;color:#315e87}.decision-brief h2{font-size:1.25rem;line-height:1.25;margin:12px 0}.decision-brief dl{margin:0}.decision-brief dl div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:145px 1fr;gap:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6ebf0;padding:9px 0}.decision-brief dt{font-size:.75rem;display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;font-weight:600}.decision-brief dt :global(.icon){color:#496fa0}.decision-brief dd{margin:0;font-size:.73rem;color:#60718a;line-height:1.65}.advisory-option h3{margin:20px 0 12px}.advisory-output{border-top:1px solid #dce5ef;padding-top:18px;margin-top:24px;font-size:.8rem}.advisory-output p{margin-top:8px}@media(max-width:900px){.launchpad-hero{gap:25px}.decision-brief{margin:12px 0 0 18px;padding:20px}.decision-brief dl div{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:5px}}@media(max-width:700px){.launchpad-hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding-top:26px}.launchpad-intro h1{font-size:2.2rem}.launchpad-workspace{padding-bottom:0}.launchpad-intro{padding-top:0}.launchpad-workspace :global(.art img){aspect-ratio:1.65}.decision-brief{margin:0 12px}.launchpad-intro .lede{font-size:.93rem}.launchpad-intro .actions{gap:18px}}
</style>
